# .understandignore — patterns for files/dirs to exclude from analysis
# Syntax: same as .gitignore (globs, # comments, ! negation, trailing / for dirs)
#
# This repo is ~104k files, but ~99% is vendored or runtime output.
# The authored project is ~55 files. The patterns below scope analysis to
# real source and exclude everything vendored, generated, or sensitive.

# --- Vendored dependency trees ---
.venv/
**/.venv/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Runtime data, conversation logs, benchmark output ---
**/chat/conversations/
**/chat/.gradio/
**/chat/serve_logs/
**/results/
**/artifacts/
**/log/
# NOTE: rngd-npu/run_all/ is NOT runtime output — it is the rngd-npu Python
# implementation that run_all.sh invokes (mirrors bench-gpu). It is included.
*.log
*.jsonl
*.diff
*.gz
*.br

# --- Binary / large assets ---
*.pdf
*.pptx
*.ttf
*.woff
*.woff2
*.map
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.svg
*.ico
*.mat

# --- Secrets ---
**/.share_login.txt

# --- Lockfiles ---
package-lock.json
*.lock

# --- Tool / meta dirs (self-referential) ---
.claude/
.understand-anything/
